# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
AuthKey*
*.p8
offline-knowledge/*

# Operator roster — real emails/identities are PII; never in the (public) repo.
# Real roster lives locally (or AISHA_OPERATORS env); only the placeholder
# example is committed. provision-operators.mjs resolves live Keycloak subs.
config/operators.json
!config/operators.json.example

# Real production-data SQL migrations — PII / PHI; never in the (public) repo.
# The folder's README promises this protection; enforce it here. Only the
# skeleton (README + .gitkeep) is tracked; any *.sql dropped in stays local.
aisha/db/seed/realdata/*
!aisha/db/seed/realdata/.gitkeep
!aisha/db/seed/realdata/README.md

# PKI — private keys and CA material
config/pki-client.key
config/pki/*.key
config/pki/root-ca.pem
openxpki-config/config.d/system/crypto.yaml
# All TLS material is regenerated per-instance by pki-init (Dockerfile.pki-init
# entrypoint, openssl). Volume `pki-config-rendered` persists across restarts.
# Keys NEVER live in git — even sample/dummy ones.
openxpki-config/tls/

trash
.aisha
.evymo

# Per-tenant / private deploy artifacts — local-only, must never be in the public
# OSS tree. Onboard tenants via overlays / scripts/init-new-tenant.sh, not here.
# Default-deny every manifest, then re-include ONLY the platform/fork stacks by
# name (safe — they are the product, not tenants). Any per-tenant manifest is
# thus ignored WITHOUT the .gitignore having to name a real tenant.
coolify/manifests/*.manifest
!coolify/manifests/_template.manifest
!coolify/manifests/aisha.manifest
!coolify/manifests/cosmos.manifest
!coolify/manifests/netbird.manifest
scripts/gen_seed_stories.py
scripts/seed_*.py

# Private tenant roster for the leak-detection gates (exact tenant names). Held
# only on operator/CI hosts — a committed denylist of real customers would itself
# disclose them. See config/tenant.json.example + src/tests/gates/lib/tenant-leak-detect.ts.
config/tenant.json

# Private/heritage instance assets — real family/company imagery, local-only,
# never in the public OSS tree (no code references them).
src/assets/eko-*.jpg
src/assets/rakusanovi.jpg
# .forgejo/ runner state + cached secrets stay out of git, but the workflows
# subtree IS source-controlled — pipelines live in git so review applies to
# them like any code. Same pattern as .claude/{commands,skills,...} below.
# Note: cannot say `.forgejo` then negate `!.forgejo/workflows/` — git stops
# recursing into excluded directories, so children can't be re-included.
# Instead, ignore only specific subpaths.
.forgejo/runner-cache/
.forgejo/secrets/
.forgejo/.runner

# Local warmup generated artifacts
docker-compose.local.generated.json
.env.local.dev

# Cold-start runtime artifacts
.coolify-deploy-snapshots/
.tmp/
.metrics/
# .claude/ — Claude Code config, mostly local-only.
# Whitelist tracked subtrees: commands (existing), skills + hooks (META-2 deploy
# target per docs/deploy/AISHA_SELF_TOOLING.md), settings.json (project-level).
# NOTE: settings.local.json is intentionally NOT tracked — it is per-machine
# local config that Claude Code auto-accrues machine-specific permission grants
# into (absolute /Users/<name>/… paths). Keep shared settings in settings.json.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/lib/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/statusline.sh

